0,Quechua Music - Melodigging,https://www.melodigging.com/genre/quechua-music,"Chimayche melodies often sit in minor or Dorian inflections, with vocal lines that alternate between Quechua and Spanish and emphasize courtship, local festivities, and highland life. Danced in couples or small circles, the style carries a dignified, unhurried pulse compared with brisker Ancashino forms, making it an emblem of the Conchucos musical identity.","Quechua, Southern Conchucos",Quechuan
1,"Quechua, Southern Conchucos Language (QXO) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level & Official Use | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/qxo/,"Southern Conchucos Quechua is a stable indigenous language of Peru. It belongs to the Quechuan language family and is part of the Quechua macrolanguage. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.","Quechua, Southern Conchucos",Quechuan
2,"Quechua, Southern Conchucos language resources | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/languages/qxo,"Quechua, Southern Conchucos language resources. Listing of people groups speaking Quechua, Southern Conchucos. Quechua, Southern Conchucos dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability.","Quechua, Southern Conchucos",Quechuan
3,Music of the Americas: Quechua Voices from Peru | AS/COA,https://www.as-coa.org/articles/music-americas-quechua-voices-peru,"April 5, 2021 - From Cusco, Ccahuana sent us her solo version of ""Apu Jesucristo,"" a sacred hymn in Quechua which is sung in a variety of festivities in the southern Peruvian Andes.","Quechua, Southern Conchucos",Quechuan
4,Conchucos Quechua | Endangered Languages Project,https://endangeredlanguages.com/elp-language/8113,"Corongo Ancash Quechua, Sihuas Ancash Quechua, Northern Conchucos Ancash Quechua, Northern Conchucos Quechua, and Southern Conchucos Ancash Quechua","Quechua, Southern Conchucos",Quechuan
5,Quechua people Facts For Kids,https://www.diy.org/article/quechua_people,"During this celebration, people wear colorful clothes, dance, and perform rituals thanking the sun for its warmth. They also have unique music, using instruments like pan flutes and drums.","Quechua, Southern Conchucos",Quechuan
